      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The passage addresses a priest or worshipper and tells this addressee to keep company with Good Mind, Righteousness the Best, and Khshathra-vairya, and to speak the praise of the Yasna to the male and female disciples of Zarathuitra Spitama.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "Zarathuitra is asked to declare words for sacrifice and worship so that waters, plants, the Fravashis of the saints, and the heavenly and earthly Yazads may be sacrificed to.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The speaker confesses being a Mazda-worshipper and gives praise, propitiation, and sacrifice to Thraetaona the Athwyan and to his Fravashi.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The text asks to be free from the dog Kuro, the Tarewani, and the Karpan.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Good thoughts, words, and deeds are said to be thought, spoken, and done with intelligence.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Evil thoughts, words, and deeds are said to be thought, spoken, and done with folly.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Those who think, speak, and do good are said to inhabit Heaven, while those who do evil are said to abide in Hell.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The Airyama-ishyo is proclaimed the greatest authoritative prayer and helpful for progress, and the Saoshyants are asked to use and revere it.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Ahura Mazda says he will rule as sovereign over his creatures, and Angra Mainyu and the Daevas are to be hidden beneath the earth.",
