    "start": "6148",
    "end": "6191",
    "translation": "The Zend-Avesta, Part III: The Yasna, Visparad, Afrinagan, Gahs, and Miscellaneous Fragments",
    "notes": "Stable markdown line range generated from canonical text."
  },
  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "The passage presents a thankful prophet addressing Ahura, describes proper offerings as righteous actions, prayer, and praise rather than sacrificial animals or fruits, mentions a meat-offering and Fire, compares Fire to Agni in a priestly function, and frames the divine Kingdom and proper prayer as oriented toward sanctity, holy action, and nourishment of the poor rather than priestly, princely, or poetic gain.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The passage says that a tone of thankfulness continues and that the prophet speaks in gratitude for better fortunes.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The prophet declares that he will bestow upon Ahura according to the measure of the gifts he has received.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The received gifts are named as secured immortality, the Righteous Order, and the Sovereign Power established in holiness and bestowing universal weal.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The proposed offerings are said to be not sacrificial beasts or fruits but the actions of the pious citizen, the homage of prayer, and songs of praise.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Ceremonial punctuality is described as being conceived together with honour and charity.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "A meat-offering is described as offered with homage to the Righteous Order and the Divine Sovereignty for sacred settlements, to equip the wise man fully, and as a blessing among the Immortals and their adherents.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Fire is mentioned and is described chiefly in comparison to Agni as the priest of the church rather than mainly as a friendly god of hearth and altar.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Fire is called upon for inward spiritual strength, temporal blessings, and vengeance likened to something hurled like a thunderbolt.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The speaker rhetorically asks what God's Kingdom is and what kind of prayer he must use so that he may become God's in his actions.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The speaker rejects loading the priesthood with sacrifices, fattening princes with booty, or securing a heavy gift to the poet, and instead speaks of nourishing the poor.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    }
  ],
